  "ssriPageTitle": "SSRI Recovery",
  "ssriHeaderStarted": "Your Recovery Journey",
  "ssriHeaderNotStarted": "Benefits of Tapering Off SSRIs",
  "ssriSubtitleStarted": "Track your progress and celebrate each milestone",
  "ssriSubtitleNotStarted": "See what happens when you taper off",
  "ssriMilestone3Title": "Day three: take it easy",
  "ssriMilestone3Description": "SSRI discontinuation can bring dizziness, nausea, insomnia and 'brain zaps'. Symptoms vary by medicine and taper. Contact your prescriber if they're difficult.",
  "ssriMilestone7Title": "One week after stopping",
  "ssriMilestone7Description": "Seven days. Some symptoms may be easing; others may only now be noticeable, especially with longer-acting medicines. You don't have to push through alone.",
  "ssriMilestone14Title": "Two weeks, check in",
  "ssriMilestone14Description": "Two weeks after stopping. Dizziness, sleep trouble or mood changes may be improving, but symptoms can last longer. Your care plan still matters.",
  "ssriMilestone30Title": "A month after the taper",
  "ssriMilestone30Description": "A month since stopping your SSRI. Sleep and mood may be settling, or you may need more support. Neither says anything bad about your progress.",
  "ssriMilestone90Title": "Three months: a checkpoint",
  "ssriMilestone90Description": "In the ANTLER trial, the difference in withdrawal symptoms was largest around twelve weeks, then narrowed later. Three months is a good time to check how you're actually feeling.",
  "ssriMilestone180Title": "Six months, your own pace",
  "ssriMilestone180Description": "Six months after stopping. One follow-up found around 65% of participants with available data remained well, but the result isn't a promise for everyone.",
  "ssriMilestone365Title": "One year after the taper",
  "ssriMilestone365Description": "A full year. In research, many people stayed well after stopping, though relapse was more common than with maintenance treatment. If you're doing well, that's worth recognising.",
  "settingsShowSsriTracking": "Show SSRI tracking",
  "settingsNotifySsri": "Notify SSRI quitting progress",
  "addictionSnri": "SNRIs",
