  "pornographyReferenceDay1095": "Three Years: Built to Last\n\nSource: Ince et al., Compulsive sexual behavior disorder (CSBD) and problematic pornography use (PPU): a comprehensive, interdisciplinary, and expert-informed narrative review (2026).\n\nCurrent evidence does not define a three-year biological endpoint for problematic pornography use. Clinical attention stays on control, distress, impairment, context, and functioning.\n\nThree years is evidence of durability. A pattern maintained across changing routines and life circumstances is worth protecting even without a universal biological countdown.",
